---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<section class="mb-5">
		<h1>PIXEL CO2</h1>
		<p class="text-xl bg-[#EEE8E0] px-2">PRE-TREATMENT INFORMATION &amp; INSTRUCTIONS</p>
	</section>
	<section>
		<div class="separation">
			<p>Thank you for your visit, it was a pleasure meeting you. Today we discussed treatment options like the CO2/ Pixel Peel. Below are a few pre-treatment considerations; if applicable.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Hyperpigmentation Prevention</h2>
			<p>Patients with darker skin tones (especially Fitzpatrick skin types IV–V), If recommended by your provider, hydroquinone 4% may be used twice daily for 4–6 weeks before treatment to reduce the risk of post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation. Then Stop HQ 1 week prior to treatment.</p>
			<p>Topical retinoids (such as tretinoin) and glycolic acid products may improve treatment preparation; however, these products are typically discontinued 5–7 days before treatment unless otherwise directed.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Cold Sore Prevention</h2>
			<p>Patients with a history of cold sores (HSV-1) may be prescribed antiviral medication (such as valacyclovir) beginning 24 hours before treatment and continuing for the duration recommended by your provider.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Please note:</h2>
			<p>	● Stop all skin retinoids/actives 7 days prior to treatment. <br>
				● You can not be on antibiotics 14 days prior to treatment. <br>
				● Avoid tanning and excessive sun exposure for at least 2–4 weeks before treatment. <br>
				● Daily use of a Mineral SPF 50 sunscreen is strongly recommended. <br>
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Contraindications for Treatment</h2>
			<p>Patients should not be considered for laser skin resurfacing procedures if they:</p>
			<p>	• Have taken Acutane® (Isotretinoin) within the past 9- 12 months <br>
				• Have a history of keloid formation <br>
				• Have a history of poor wound healing <br>
				• Epilepsy <br>
				• Antibiotic or Steroid in the past 2 weeks <br>
				• Active bacterial or viral infections <br>
				• Demonstrate excessive or unusually prolonged erythema, hyperpigmentation, or hypopigmentation upon laser test patching <br>
				• Pregnancy and breastfeeding <br>
				• Cancer in the past 6 months, Chemo/radiation in the past 6 months <br>
				• Botox in the past 2 weeks/ Filler in past 4 weeks <br>
				• PDO treads in the past 8 weeks <br>
				• Any ablative treatment in the area in the past 4 weeks <br>
				• Impaired immune system <br>
				• Scleroderma <br>
				• Extensive radiation therapy <br>
				• Burns in treatment area <br>
				• Skin type VI <br>
			</p>
			<p>Other possible contraindications may include irregular pigmentation of the skin (lentigo maligna, melanoma, acanthuses nigricans), Lichen Planus, Vitiligo or Psoriasis.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Expectations</h2>
			<p>Following CO₂ resurfacing, redness, swelling, warmth, and peeling are expected.</p>
			<p>Recovery time varies based on treatment intensity but commonly ranges from 5–14 days.</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
